      "api_error_status": null,
      "result": "By default, `more_itertools.chunked` puts the leftover items in a **shorter final chunk**. It doesn't pad that chunk or drop any items:\n\n```python\n>>> from more_itertools import chunked\n>>> list(chunked([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], 3))\n[[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8]]\n```\n\nIf you pass `strict=True`, it raises a `ValueError` when the last chunk would be short:\n\n```python\n>>> list(chunked([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], 3, strict=True))\nValueError: iterator is not divisible by n.\n```\n\nIf you want padding instead, use `more_itertools.grouper(iterable, n, incomplete='fill', fillvalue=None)`. It fills the last group with `fillvalue`, and its default mode is `'fill'`. You can also pass `incomplete='ignore'` to drop the leftover items.",
